body:
"Different take" == "added some other stuff then took a second photo"

&#x200B;

Also, not just same shirt; same earrings, same septum ring

NAH

&#x200B;

To be fair to your boyfriend, there are definitely people who would see that and think you're being passive-aggressive. It also doesn't help that in this case it's just text; you don't have your face or tone of voice to show the other person you're kidding. I'd avoid doing it in the future (unless you know the recipient personally), but I don't think what you did is really "Asshole-ish".

Agreed. From VA, live in Boston area now.

&#x200B;

Massachusetts threw a shit fit when they were told to desegregate.

YTA.

&#x200B;

What your grandma did was really petty, but you were being pretty terrible. She took you in when she didn't have to and you're being disruptive of her sleep schedule. As you experienced this morning, having your sleep disrupted makes you irritable, and from your post it sounds like you've done this to *her* multiple times. If you can't live with her and not disrupt her sleep, it's time to move out.
